NOTE: ============================================================
NOTE: Comprehensive HPL Test File
NOTE: Tests every grammar construct, operator, and edge case
NOTE: ============================================================

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 1. Variable Declarations (all types)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Let counter be number.
Let total be number.
Let limit be number.
Let flag be number.
Let result be number.
Let greeting be text.
Let name be text.
Let emptyText be text.
Let charResult be text.

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 2. Assignment - Set ... to
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set counter to 0.
Set total to 100.
Set limit to 10.
Set flag to 1.
Set greeting to "Hello".
Set name to "World".
Set emptyText to "".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 3. Arithmetic assignments
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Increase counter by 1.
Increase total by 50.
Decrease total by 25.
Multiply counter by 3.
Divide total by 5.

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 4. Expressions - additive ops
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set result to counter plus 10.
Set result to total minus 20.
Set result to 5 plus 3 minus 1.
Set result to counter plus total minus limit.

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 5. Expressions - multiplicative ops
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set result to counter times 2.
Set result to total divide 4.
Set result to 3 times 5 plus 2.
Set result to 2 plus 3 times 5.
Set result to counter times limit divide 2.

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 6. Expressions - remainderOf ... dividedBy
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set result to remainderOf 17 dividedBy 5.
Set result to remainderOf counter dividedBy 3.
Set result to remainderOf total dividedBy limit.

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 7. Expressions - parenthesised
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set result to (5 plus 3) times 2.
Set result to 10 minus (2 plus 3).
Set result to (counter plus 1) times (limit minus 2).
Set result to ((5 plus 3) times 2) minus 1.

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 8. Negative numbers
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set result to -1.
Set result to -42 plus 50.
Set result to 10 plus -3.

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 10. IO - Show (numbers and text)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Show counter.
Show "\n".
Show total.
Show "\n".
Show result.
Show "\n".
Show greeting.
Show "\n".
Show "Literal string output".
Show "\n".
Show counter plus 1.
Show "\n".
Show (counter times 2) plus 1.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 11. IO - Get (moved to end, requires input)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: Get statements are tested at the very end since they block for input.
NOTE: For now, simulate the result:
Set counter to 3.
Set name to "Tester".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 12. atPosition - text indexing (1-based)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set greeting to "ABCDE".
Set charResult to greeting atPosition (1).
Show charResult.
Show "\n".
Set charResult to greeting atPosition (5).
Show charResult.
Show "\n".
Set charResult to greeting atPosition (counter plus 1).
Show charResult.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 13. atPosition - assignment to character
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set greeting atPosition (1) to "Z".
Show greeting.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 14. If / then (simple)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If counter greaterThan 0 then:
    Show "Counter is positive".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 15. If / Otherwise (else)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If counter equalsTo 0 then:
    Show "Counter is zero".
    Show "\n".
Otherwise:
    Show "Counter is not zero".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 16. If / Otherwise if / Otherwise (else-if chain)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If counter greaterThan 100 then:
    Show "High".
    Show "\n".
Otherwise if counter greaterThan 50 then:
    Show "Medium".
    Show "\n".
Otherwise if counter greaterThan 0 then:
    Show "Low".
    Show "\n".
Otherwise:
    Show "Zero or negative".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 17. Relational operators (all 6)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If counter equalsTo 0 then:
    Show "equalsTo works".
    Show "\n".
If counter notEqualsTo 99 then:
    Show "notEqualsTo works".
    Show "\n".
If counter greaterThan -1 then:
    Show "greaterThan works".
    Show "\n".
If counter lessThan 1000 then:
    Show "lessThan works".
    Show "\n".
If counter atLeast 0 then:
    Show "atLeast works".
    Show "\n".
If counter atMost 999 then:
    Show "atMost works".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 18. Compound conditions - and
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If counter atLeast 0 and counter atMost 100 then:
    Show "Counter in range 0-100".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 19. Compound conditions - or
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If counter equalsTo 0 or counter equalsTo 1 then:
    Show "Counter is 0 or 1".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 20. Compound conditions - and + or combined
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If counter equalsTo 0 or counter greaterThan 5 and counter lessThan 50 then:
    Show "Complex condition passed".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 21. Negated conditions - not
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If not counter equalsTo 99 then:
    Show "Counter is not 99".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 22. Parenthesised conditions
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If (counter equalsTo 0 or counter equalsTo 1) and flag equalsTo 1 then:
    Show "Grouped condition passed".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 23. Nested if statements
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If counter atLeast 0 then:
    If counter atMost 10 then:
        Show "Counter is 0-10".
        Show "\n".
    Otherwise:
        Show "Counter is above 10".
        Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 24. Repeat loop
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set counter to 0.
Repeat 5 iterations:
    Increase counter by 1.
    Show counter.
    Show "\n".
Show "After repeat loop".
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 25. Repeat with expression
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set limit to 3.
Repeat limit iterations:
    Show "Looping".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 26. While loop
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set counter to 5.
While counter greaterThan 0:
    Show counter.
    Show "\n".
    Decrease counter by 1.
Show "While loop done".
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 27. While with compound condition
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set counter to 0.
Show "Hello".
While counter lessThan 10 and flag equalsTo 1:
    Increase counter by 1.    

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 28. Nested loops
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set counter to 0.
Repeat 3 iterations:
    Repeat 2 iterations:
        Increase counter by 1.
Show counter.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 29. Loop with if inside
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set counter to 0.
Repeat 10 iterations:
    Increase counter by 1.
    If remainderOf counter dividedBy 2 equalsTo 0 then:
        Show "Even".
        Show "\n".
    Otherwise:
        Show "Odd".
        Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 30. Function declaration (no parameters)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To sayHello with nan:
    Show "Hello from function!".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 31. Function call (no arguments)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
sayHello with (nan).

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 32. Function with one parameter
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To doubleIt with x:
    Let result be number.
    Set result to x times 2.
    Return result.

Set result to doubleIt with (5).
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 33. Function with multiple parameters
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To addThree with a, b, c:
    Return a plus b plus c.

Set result to addThree with (10, 20, 30).
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 34. Function with local variables
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To computeArea with width, height:
    Let area be number.
    Set area to width times height.
    Return area.

Set result to computeArea with (6, 7).
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 35. Function with conditional logic
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To absValue with n:
    If n lessThan 0 then:
        Set n to 0 minus n.
    Return n.

Set result to absValue with (-42).
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 36. Function with loop
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To factorial with n:
    Let acc be number.
    Set acc to 1.
    While n greaterThan 1:
        Multiply acc by n.
        Decrease n by 1.
    Return acc.

Set result to factorial with (5).
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 37. Function calling another function
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To tripleIt with x:
    Return x times 3.

To doubleThenTriple with x:
    Let res be number.
    Set res to doubleIt with (x).
    Set res to tripleIt with (res).
    Return res.

Set result to doubleThenTriple with (4).
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 38. Recursive function
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To fibonacci with n:
    If n atMost 1 then:
        Return n.
    Return fibonacci with (n minus 1) plus fibonacci with (n minus 2).

Set result to fibonacci with (10).
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 39. Function with text parameter
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To greet with who:
    Show "Hello, ".
    Show who.
    Show "!".
    Show "\n".

greet with ("HPL").

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 40. Function with IO
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To askAndDouble with nan:
    Let val be number.
    Set val to 21.
    Return val times 2.

Set result to askAndDouble with (nan).
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 41. Function returning text
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To makeGreeting with first, last:
    Show first.
    Show " ".
    Show last.
    Show "\n".

makeGreeting with ("John", "Doe").

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 42. Void function (no return)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To printBanner with nan:
    Show "====================".
    Show "\n".
    Show "   HPL Test Suite   ".
    Show "\n".
    Show "====================".
    Show "\n".

printBanner with (nan).

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 43. Complex expression as function argument
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set result to doubleIt with ((3 plus 4) times 2).
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 44. Multiple statements in block
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
If 1 equalsTo 1 then:
    Let temp be number.
    Set temp to 42.
    Increase temp by 8.
    Show temp.
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 45. Deeply nested blocks
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set counter to 5.
If counter greaterThan 0 then:
    If counter greaterThan 2 then:
        If counter greaterThan 4 then:
            Show "Deeply nested: counter > 4".
            Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 46. Long elif chain
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set counter to 3.
If counter equalsTo 1 then:
    Show "One".
    Show "\n".
Otherwise if counter equalsTo 2 then:
    Show "Two".
    Show "\n".
Otherwise if counter equalsTo 3 then:
    Show "Three".
    Show "\n".
Otherwise if counter equalsTo 4 then:
    Show "Four".
    Show "\n".
Otherwise if counter equalsTo 5 then:
    Show "Five".
    Show "\n".
Otherwise:
    Show "Other".
    Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 47. Expression in Show
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Show 2 plus 3 times 4.
Show "\n".
Show (2 plus 3) times 4.
Show "\n".
Show remainderOf 100 dividedBy 7.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 48. Chained string concatenation in Show
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Set name to "HPL".
Show "Language: ".
Show name.
Show " v1.0".
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 49. Stress test - many variables
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Let v1 be number.
Let v2 be number.
Let v3 be number.
Let v4 be number.
Let v5 be number.
Set v1 to 1.
Set v2 to 2.
Set v3 to 3.
Set v4 to 4.
Set v5 to 5.
Set result to v1 plus v2 plus v3 plus v4 plus v5.
Show result.
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 50. Final comprehensive test
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
To sumRange with low, high:
    Let s be number.
    Set s to 0.
    While low atMost high:
        Increase s by low.
        Increase low by 1.
    Return s.

Set result to sumRange with (1, 100).
Show result.
Show "\n".

Show "All non-interactive tests complete.".
Show "\n".

NOTE: ----------------------------------------
NOTE: 51. IO - Get (interactive, runs last)
NOTE: ----------------------------------------
Get number ask "Enter a number: " storeInto counter.
Show counter.
Show "\n".
Get text ask "Enter your name: " storeInto name.
Show "Hello, ".
Show name.
Show "!".
Show "\n".
Show "All tests complete.".
Show "\n".
